   "flags": [],
   "use": "The standard way to explain a minor illness, mostly in the past: taichou kuzushichatte (I came down with something). It fills excuses for missing work or school, and the send-off taichou kuzusanai you ni ne (look after yourself). O often drops.",
   "notes": "Taichou ga warui is the state; taichou o kuzusu is falling into it.",
   "example": {
    "romaji": "chotto taichou kuzushite, kinou yasunda.",
    "ja": "ちょっと体調崩して、昨日休んだ。",
    "english": "I got a bit run down and took yesterday off."
   },
   "examplePolite": {
    "romaji": "chotto taichou o kuzushite, kinou wa yasumimashita.",
    "ja": "ちょっと体調を崩して、昨日は休みました。",
    "english": "I was a bit under the weather, so I took yesterday off."
   }
  },
  {
